Header
  + name := Did_you_know
/*
  "Did you know?": a small card on the desktop with a tip about Lisaac Ω,
  a new one each day. A click on the card shows the next tip, a click on
  "Lisaac Ω · lisaac.org" opens the web site. Drag the card to move it,
  Escape closes it.

  Add your own tips at the end of @tips: a tip is a title, then the text
  (a "\n" goes to the next line).

  Shows: a @Gadget, an @Array of @String_alias written in one go, the
  number of the day computed from the clock (@Clock.time_raw).

  To compile, as usual in a terminal:
  $ lisaac did_you_know -q -boost
  $ ./did_you_know
  */
Inherit

  + parent_gadget:Flat Gadget

Public

  - draw <-
  ( + b:Real32
    b := 8
    // The card, with its shadow.
    begin_path
    rect (b + 4,b + 6) size (width - 2 * b,height - 2 * b) radius 14
    fill_color (Color.rgba (0,0,0,60))
    fill
    begin_path
    rect (b,b) size (width - 2 * b,height - 2 * b) radius 14
    fill_color (Color.rgb (225,238,255))
    fill
    // The Ω in a circle, and the title.
    begin_path
    circle (b + 34,b + 34) radius 20
    fill_color (Color.rgb (40,90,170))
    fill
    font_face_id (Font.sys (Font.bold))
    font_size 28
    text_align (align_center | align_middle)
    fill_color white
    text (b + 34,b + 35) msg "Ω"
    font_size 24
    text_align (align_left | align_middle)
    fill_color (Color.rgb (40,90,170))
    text (b + 64,b + 34) msg "Did you know?"
    // The tip: its title, then its text.
    font_size 20
    text_align (align_left | align_top)
    fill_color (Color.rgb (30,30,30))
    text_box (b + 18,b + 70) width (width - 2 * b - 36) msg (tips.at (2 * current))
    font_face_id (Font.sys (Font.roman))
    font_size 18
    text_box (b + 18,b + 100) width (width - 2 * b - 36) msg (tips.at (2 * current + 1))
    signature (width / 2,height - b - 12)
  )

  - event ev:Int :Boolean <-
  (
    (((ev & ~1) = Hand.clic) && {! is_on_signature}).if {
      current := (current + 1) % count
      Paper.refresh_again
    }
    parent_gadget.event ev
  )

  - main <-
  (
    // One tip by day: the number of days since 1970, modulo the number of tips.
    current := (Clock.time_raw / (24 * 60 * 60)).to_int % count
    show "Did you know? · Lisaac Ω" size (440,300)
  )

Private

  - current:Int

  - count:Int <- tips.count / 2

  - tips:Array String_alias := new Array String_alias of (
    "No keyword for the control flow",
    "if, while or foreach are methods of True, False or Block, written in the library:\n  (x > 0).if { ... } else { ... }",
    "Integers without limit",
    "ℤ never overflows: 100! or 2^200 are exact. ℚ is exact too: 1/3 + 1/6 = 1/2.",
    "Mathematics as in the book",
    "With ℂ, you write x + i y, as in the book, and a slot may be named π.",
    "Prototypes, not classes",
    "Every object is a prototype, and clone makes a new one. Self is the prototype of self.",
    "Inherit or Insert?",
    "Inherit makes a subtype (assignment, dynamic dispatch). Insert only takes the slots: a toolbox.",
    "One line, one instruction",
    "A newline ends the instruction. To continue it on the next line, end the line with \\r\\n.",
    "Contracts",
    "A contract before the body of a method is checked at run time, and -boost removes it:\n  [ ? {n >= 0} ]",
    "Strings",
    "A String_alias is unique in the program: compare two of them with =. A String_buffer is the one you modify.",
    "Concurrency without locks",
    "With -cop, a prototype named with - is an active object: a universe with its own messages and its own slots.",
    "French corner",
    "For the very beginners:\n  répéter 4 fois { ... }\n  si (c) alors { ... } sinon { ... }",
    "From Lisaac to C",
    "lisaac hello -boost writes ANSI C, then gcc compiles it. Add --r to read the C produced.",
    "This card",
    "is 100 lines of Lisaac Ω: see example/gadgets. The post-it, the Ω eyes and the Christmas sky are there too."
  )
